# Handbook §26 — THE REPOSITORY IS THE WEB ROOT.
#
# This file is doing ACCESS CONTROL, not housekeeping. Every path below would otherwise be served
# at a URL the moment it is committed, because the deploy step is copying files.
#
# Deleting a file later does not unpublish it: it stays in edge caches and in search indexes, and
# where the repository is readable it stays in history. The remediation for an accidental commit is
# rewriting history and rotating whatever was exposed — not a deletion commit.

# Internal brand and design material — never published
Branding/
*.ai
*.psd
*.sketch
*.fig

# Archives. LOCAL ADDITION, not in templates/landing@v3.7.1 — reported as
# engineering-handbook#58. An archive is the most likely form for exactly the material the block
# above exists to keep out, because "send me the logos" produces a zip and somebody commits it next
# to the folder it came from. That is precisely what happened here: `Logos MK Sense.zip`, 583 KB,
# was downloadable at its URL for eight months while the `.ai` beside it was the one the pattern
# caught.
*.zip
*.rar
*.7z
*.tar
*.tgz
*.tar.gz

# Working versions and client material
drafts/
client/
*.docx
*.xlsx

# Local
node_modules/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.env
.env.*

# NOT ignored, on purpose: .gate-baseline.json is committed. It is the record of what this
# repository owed on the day it adopted the standard, and the ratchet compares against it.
